From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Domenico D'Arrigo <d.darrigo@outlook.it>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 19:47:54 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] sb/intel/lynxpoint: Leave the wake status to the OS on S3
 resume

smm_southbridge_clear_state() clears PM1_STS and GPE0_STS at every boot,
S3 resume included, after pch_log_state() has put the wake source in the
event log. The OS then finds no wake source: Linux reads the power
button status on resume to report a wakeup event, and macOS decides by
these registers whether a wake is a full one, by the user, or a dark
wake (pmset reports the wake reason from them).

On S3 resume, leave PM1_STS and GPE0_STS to the OS, which clears them.
Set SCI_EN first, as the OS had it before it slept: SCI_EN is written
again only in lpc_init(), after global_smi_enable() has enabled the
power button and the SMIs, and with SCI_EN clear a pending power button
event would raise an SMI, which southbridge_smi_pm1() turns into a power
off, and a pending GPE an SMI that clears GPE0_STS.

TEST=Built lenovo/w541 with mrc.bin and with the native RAM init.

Co-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018n3yuWwDLW63F4vdf7ZFTv
---
 src/southbridge/intel/lynxpoint/smi.c | 19 +++++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 17 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/southbridge/intel/lynxpoint/smi.c b/src/southbridge/intel/lynxpoint/smi.c
index 5f7d48af77..37d2008a26 100644
--- a/src/southbridge/intel/lynxpoint/smi.c
+++ b/src/southbridge/intel/lynxpoint/smi.c
@@ -1,5 +1,6 @@
 /* SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-only */
 
+#include <acpi/acpi.h>
 #include <device/device.h>
 #include <device/pci.h>
 #include <console/console.h>
@@ -28,9 +29,23 @@ void smm_southbridge_clear_state(void)
 
 	/* Dump and clear status registers */
 	clear_smi_status();
-	clear_pm1_status();
 	clear_tco_status();
-	clear_gpe_status();
+
+	/*
+	 * On S3 resume PM1_STS and GPE0_STS hold the wake source: leave them to
+	 * the OS, which reads and clears them (macOS tells a wake by the user
+	 * from a dark wake by them). Their events go to the OS as SCIs, as
+	 * before it slept: with SCI_EN clear, the SMIs enabled next would take
+	 * them, and the SMI handler turns a pending power button event into a
+	 * power off.
+	 */
+	if (acpi_is_wakeup_s3()) {
+		enable_pm1_control(SCI_EN);
+		printk(BIOS_DEBUG, "S3 resume: PM1 and GPE0 status left to the OS\n");
+	} else {
+		clear_pm1_status();
+		clear_gpe_status();
+	}
 }
 
 static void smm_southbridge_enable(uint16_t pm1_events)
